WEBVTT

00:00.570 --> 00:04.470
We're asked to solve the
right triangle shown below.

00:04.470 --> 00:07.140
Give the lengths to
the nearest tenth.

00:07.140 --> 00:08.920
So when they say solve
the right triangle,

00:08.920 --> 00:09.810
we can assume that
they're saying,

00:09.810 --> 00:11.680
hey figure out the
lengths of all the sides.

00:11.680 --> 00:14.500
So whatever a is equal to,
whatever b is equal to.

00:14.500 --> 00:17.180
And also what are all the
angles of the right triangle?

00:17.180 --> 00:18.410
They've given two of them.

00:18.410 --> 00:21.550
We might have to figure out
this third right over here.

00:21.550 --> 00:24.070
So there's multiple
ways to tackle this,

00:24.070 --> 00:28.460
but we'll just try to
tackle side XW first,

00:28.460 --> 00:30.920
try to figure out what a is.

00:30.920 --> 00:32.229
And I'll give you a hint.

00:32.229 --> 00:34.600
You can use a calculator,
and using a calculator,

00:34.600 --> 00:36.540
you can use your
trigonometric functions

00:36.540 --> 00:38.735
that we've looked
at a good bit now.

00:38.735 --> 00:40.360
So I'll give you a
few seconds to think

00:40.360 --> 00:45.629
about how to figure
out what a is.

00:45.630 --> 00:47.090
Well, what do we know?

00:47.090 --> 00:49.610
We know this angle
y right over here.

00:49.610 --> 00:52.839
We know the side
adjacent to angle y.

00:52.840 --> 00:55.410
And length a, this
is the side that's

00:55.410 --> 01:00.699
the length of the side that
is opposite to angle Y.

01:00.700 --> 01:04.239
So what trigonometric
ratio deals

01:04.239 --> 01:06.680
with the opposite
and the adjacent?

01:06.680 --> 01:08.990
So if we're looking at angle
Y, relative to angle Y,

01:08.990 --> 01:10.910
this is the opposite.

01:10.910 --> 01:14.024
And this right over
here is the adjacent.

01:14.024 --> 01:16.315
Well if we don't remember,
we can go back to SohCahToa.

01:21.240 --> 01:23.660
Sine deals with
opposite and hypotenuse.

01:23.660 --> 01:26.420
Cosine deals with
adjacent and hypotenuse.

01:26.420 --> 01:29.320
Tangent deals with
opposite over adjacent.

01:31.890 --> 01:38.150
So we can say that the
tangent of 65 degrees,

01:38.150 --> 01:42.250
of that angle of 65 degrees,
is equal to the opposite,

01:42.250 --> 01:44.050
the length of the
opposite side, which

01:44.050 --> 01:48.750
we know has length a over the
length of the adjacent side,

01:48.750 --> 01:53.170
which they gave us in the
diagram, which has length five.

01:53.170 --> 01:55.010
And you might say,
how do I figure out a?

01:55.010 --> 01:57.350
Well we can use our
calculator to evaluate

01:57.350 --> 01:59.734
what the tangent
of 65 degrees are.

01:59.734 --> 02:00.899
And then we can solve for a.

02:00.900 --> 02:04.320
And actually if we just want to
get the expression explicitly

02:04.320 --> 02:05.960
solving for a, we
could just multiply

02:05.960 --> 02:08.500
both sides of this
equation times 5.

02:08.500 --> 02:09.930
So let's do that.

02:09.930 --> 02:13.120
5 times, times 5.

02:13.120 --> 02:15.410
These cancel out,
and we are left with,

02:15.410 --> 02:18.230
if we flip the
equal around, we're

02:18.230 --> 02:26.489
left with a is equal to 5 times
the tangent of 65 degrees.

02:26.490 --> 02:28.780
So now we can get our
calculator out and figure out

02:28.780 --> 02:31.760
what this is to
the nearest tenth.

02:31.760 --> 02:41.733
That's my handy TI-85 out and
I have 5 times the tangent--

02:41.734 --> 02:43.900
I didn't need to press that
second right over there,

02:43.900 --> 02:48.890
just a regular
tangent-- of 65 degrees.

02:48.890 --> 02:52.649
And I will get, if I
round to the nearest tenth

02:52.650 --> 02:55.800
like they ask me to, I get 10.7.

02:55.800 --> 03:01.290
So a is approximately
equal to 10.7.

03:01.290 --> 03:05.730
I say approximately
because I rounded it down.

03:05.730 --> 03:07.519
This is not the exact number.

03:07.520 --> 03:09.870
But a is equal to 10.7.

03:09.870 --> 03:14.070
So we now know that this has
length 10.7, approximately.

03:14.070 --> 03:17.450
There are several ways that
we can try to tackle b.

03:17.450 --> 03:19.290
And I'll let you pick
the way you want to.

03:19.290 --> 03:21.420
But then I'll just do it
the way I would like to.

03:21.420 --> 03:23.890
So my next question
to you is, what

03:23.890 --> 03:28.829
is the length of the side YW?

03:28.830 --> 03:31.560
Or what is the value of b?

03:34.229 --> 03:35.770
Well there are
several ways to do it.

03:35.770 --> 03:36.860
This is the hypotenuse.

03:36.860 --> 03:38.900
So we could use
trigonometric functions

03:38.900 --> 03:41.510
that deal with adjacent
over hypotenuse or opposite

03:41.510 --> 03:42.840
over hypotenuse.

03:42.840 --> 03:45.750
Or we could just use
the Pythagorean theorem.

03:45.750 --> 03:47.770
We know two sides
of a right triangle.

03:47.770 --> 03:50.320
We can come up with
the third side.

03:50.320 --> 03:54.799
I will go with using
trigonometric ratios

03:54.800 --> 03:57.280
since that's what we've
been working on a good bit.

03:57.280 --> 04:01.710
So this length of b, that's
the length of the hypotenuse.

04:01.710 --> 04:07.734
So this side WY
is the hypotenuse.

04:07.734 --> 04:09.400
And so what trigonometric
ratios-- or we

04:09.400 --> 04:10.691
can decide what we want to use.

04:10.691 --> 04:12.500
We could use opposite
and hypotenuse.

04:12.500 --> 04:14.660
We could use adjacent
and hypotenuse.

04:14.660 --> 04:16.427
Since we know that
XY is exactly 5

04:16.427 --> 04:18.510
and we don't have to deal
with this approximation,

04:18.510 --> 04:19.750
let's use that side.

04:19.750 --> 04:21.250
So what trigonometric
ratios deal

04:21.250 --> 04:23.850
with adjacent and hypotenuse?

04:23.850 --> 04:26.670
Well we see from
SohCahToa cosine deals

04:26.670 --> 04:30.080
with adjacent over hypotenuse.

04:30.080 --> 04:36.940
So we could say that
the cosine of 65 degrees

04:36.940 --> 04:40.090
is equal to the length of
the adjacent side, which

04:40.090 --> 04:44.690
is 5 over the length of
the hypotenuse, which

04:44.690 --> 04:46.910
has a length of b.

04:46.910 --> 04:49.010
And then we can
try to solve for b.

04:49.010 --> 04:51.120
You multiply both
sides times b, you're

04:51.120 --> 04:56.910
left with b times cosine of
65 degrees is equal to 5.

04:56.910 --> 04:59.290
And then to solve for b,
you could divide both sides

04:59.290 --> 05:01.910
by cosine of 65 degrees.

05:01.910 --> 05:03.100
This is just a number here.

05:03.100 --> 05:04.820
So we're just dividing--
we have to figure it

05:04.820 --> 05:06.570
out what our calculator,
but this is just

05:06.570 --> 05:08.120
going to evaluate
to some number.

05:08.120 --> 05:12.950
So we can divide both sides by
that, by cosine of 65 degrees.

05:16.680 --> 05:20.290
And we're left with
b is equal to 5

05:20.290 --> 05:24.470
over the cosine of 65 degrees.

05:24.470 --> 05:27.740
So let us now use our calculator
to figure out the length of b.

05:27.740 --> 05:35.210
Length of b is 5 divided
by cosine of 65 degrees.

05:35.210 --> 05:39.719
And I get, if I round to
the nearest tenth, 11.8.

05:39.720 --> 05:43.290
So b is approximately equal
to, rounded to the nearest

05:43.290 --> 05:46.210
tenth, 11.8.

05:46.210 --> 05:50.099
So b is equal to 11.8.

05:50.100 --> 05:52.730
And then we're almost done
solving this right triangle.

05:52.730 --> 05:55.105
And you could have figured
this out using the Pythagorean

05:55.105 --> 05:57.480
theorem as well, saying that
5 squared plus 10.7 squared

05:57.480 --> 05:58.750
should be equal to b squared.

05:58.750 --> 06:00.950
And hopefully you would
get the exact same answer.

06:00.950 --> 06:02.616
And the last thing
we have to figure out

06:02.616 --> 06:07.919
is the measure of angle
W right over here.

06:07.920 --> 06:09.560
So I'll give you a
few seconds to think

06:09.560 --> 06:14.170
about what the
measure of angle W is.

06:14.170 --> 06:15.910
Well here we just
have to remember

06:15.910 --> 06:20.500
that the sum of the angles of a
triangle add up to 180 degrees.

06:20.500 --> 06:26.940
So angle w plus 65 degrees,
that's this angle right up

06:26.940 --> 06:30.420
here, plus the right angle,
this is a right triangle,

06:30.420 --> 06:34.280
they're going to add
up to 180 degrees.

06:34.280 --> 06:37.371
So all we need to do
is-- well we can simplify

06:37.372 --> 06:38.830
the left-hand side
right over here.

06:38.830 --> 06:41.539
65 plus 90 is 155.

06:41.540 --> 06:48.380
So angle W plus 155 degrees
is equal to 180 degrees.

06:48.380 --> 06:52.920
And then we get angle W-- if we
subtract 155 from both sides--

06:52.920 --> 06:57.590
angle W is equal to 25 degrees.

06:57.590 --> 07:03.123
And we are done solving the
right triangle shown below.
